{
  "chapter.44DA95F01132476A.title": "03 • Refined Storage: Working Systems",
  "task.5147BC2D367EF0E9.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.1F3926F40A6B3002.title": "Start here: Refined Storage",
  "quest.1F3926F40A6B3002.quest_subtitle": "Start Here",
  "quest.1F3926F40A6B3002.quest_desc": [
    "Refined Storage turns inventories into a searchable network and can schedule crafting through patterns and machines. This companion chapter focuses on reliable production and the installed addons. The original Refined Storage chapter still covers the basic components.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/advanced_rs.png width:330 height:150 align:center}",
    "",
    "&b&lChoose a branch&r",
    "• Autocrafting",
    "• Resource Networks",
    "• Wireless & Building",
    "",
    "Your route: working network -> machine autocrafting -> stockkeeping -> extra resource types -> wireless, kitchen and building integrations -> a dependable automated workshop.",
    "",
    "&eStart with the first equipment milestone, then follow the branch you need."
  ],
  "task.305C65653D7E7669.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.3B67BA5B0470AFBB.title": "Map legend & completion rules",
  "quest.3B67BA5B0470AFBB.quest_subtitle": "Reference",
  "quest.3B67BA5B0470AFBB.quest_desc": [
    "Follow a branch that solves your next problem. Equipment icons lead to concrete inventory milestones; the book card is a reference, and a large diamond marks a workshop project.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the setup before crafting. Item milestones detect your inventory without consuming items. Their practical checkmarks are optional reminders; final workshop projects require a practical confirmation. An item in your bag does not prove that a machine is configured. Existing equipment counts: do not rebuild a working system just for this map.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "JEI shows this pack's current recipes. Branches explain how the systems connect. Optional side projects are independent of the main route; no casino win is required."
  ],
  "task.208752D14F13BB55.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.162CDF11A62C8795.title": "A network you can explain",
  "quest.162CDF11A62C8795.quest_subtitle": "Autocrafting",
  "quest.162CDF11A62C8795.quest_desc": [
    "A controller, storage and grid have different jobs. Understanding those jobs prevents a full disk or disconnected cable from looking like a recipe bug.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build or inspect a powered network with a Controller, Disk Drive, storage disk and Grid. Insert a small stack, retrieve part of it and check capacity and energy usage.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Do not store your only network-repair materials inside a network that has no backup power."
  ],
  "task.54B2F3573647D789.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.091432FDBD674325.title": "External storage priorities",
  "quest.091432FDBD674325.quest_subtitle": "Resource Networks",
  "quest.091432FDBD674325.quest_desc": [
    "External Storage makes existing drawers or inventories visible to RS; it does not turn them into unlimited disks.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Attach External Storage to a test inventory. Check filters, access mode and priority, then insert a known stack through the grid and see where it goes.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "DRAWER PATTERN: Connect External Storage to the drawer controller, lock the intended drawer types, and give that storage a higher insertion priority than the disk store. New cobble should go to its drawer instead of filling your general-purpose disk.",
    "",
    "TEST THE FALLBACK: Insert one stack and inspect the physical drawer. Temporarily fill the target and check where further inserts go. An attached empty drawer can accept an unintended item unless its type is locked.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use a disposable test stack before linking bulk storage. Avoid letting another network expose this same network back to itself."
  ],
  "task.7A5972EFA9B89B47.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.249CA20A77338E51.title": "Encode a simple pattern",
  "quest.249CA20A77338E51.quest_subtitle": "Autocrafting",
  "quest.249CA20A77338E51.quest_desc": [
    "A pattern tells RS how inputs become outputs. Start with a normal crafting recipe before adding machines or fluids.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Use a Pattern Grid and blank Pattern to encode a simple recipe such as planks into sticks. Put it into an Autocrafter and request one craft from the grid.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep a small buffer of raw materials. A pattern does not supply ingredients on its own."
  ],
  "task.1223F4FD8CF81018.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.39894938C7D1DDFA.title": "Choose the correct recipe",
  "quest.39894938C7D1DDFA.quest_subtitle": "Autocrafting",
  "quest.39894938C7D1DDFA.quest_desc": [
    "Several mods can use the same ingredient arrangement. A wrongly encoded result can make an otherwise valid crafting network produce the wrong thing.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "In a Crafting Grid or Pattern Grid, inspect the recipe-selection button added by RS Polymorph when ingredients match multiple recipes. Choose the intended result and verify the printed pattern's output.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Test the resulting pattern once. Recipe selection solves ambiguity; it does not make missing ingredients or unavailable recipes appear."
  ],
  "task.63C581E35C0FF07A.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.21E76B3B169DDD8D.title": "Your first machine pattern",
  "quest.21E76B3B169DDD8D.quest_subtitle": "Autocrafting",
  "quest.21E76B3B169DDD8D.quest_desc": [
    "Processing patterns describe an external machine operation. The network must both deliver ingredients and receive the promised result.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Choose one simple furnace-like recipe. Encode the actual input/output amounts as a processing pattern, point an Autocrafter at the machine's input or a buffer, and return output through an Importer. Request one batch.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "WORKED EXAMPLE: Encode a processing pattern that consumes one raw basic processor and produces one basic processor. Aim the Autocrafter at the input of a furnace that accepts it. Return the furnace output through an Importer or another tested insertion path into this same network.",
    "",
    "REQUEST ONE: With raw materials in storage, request one basic processor from the Grid. Watch the raw processor leave, the furnace finish, and the finished processor return. The Autocrafting Monitor should then clear the job.",
    "",
    "WAITING FOREVER? If ingredients arrived, inspect the exact output promised by the pattern. RS cannot finish a recipe that promised two items but returns one, or whose output was sent to an unrelated chest.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep the return path separate from the input path. If results never re-enter RS, the job can remain waiting even when the machine finished.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/advanced_rs.png width:330 height:150 align:center}"
  ],
  "task.054302526DF7032B.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.2A822AF413B88804.title": "Diagnose a stalled craft",
  "quest.2A822AF413B88804.quest_subtitle": "Autocrafting",
  "quest.2A822AF413B88804.quest_desc": [
    "The monitor separates missing ingredients from a processing job that is waiting on output.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect a small job in the Autocrafting Monitor. Follow the route from pattern to machine input, power/redstone state, output slot and Importer. Correct the first failing step before retrying.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Do not repeatedly request the same stalled job. Check the queue and return any stranded ingredients before canceling or restarting."
  ],
  "task.18809C09EB5CCED1.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.232242C253C5C6A2.title": "Keep a useful item stocked",
  "quest.232242C253C5C6A2.quest_subtitle": "Autocrafting",
  "quest.232242C253C5C6A2.quest_desc": [
    "Requestify schedules crafts when stock falls below a target. It turns an on-demand recipe into a replenishment system.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Connect a Requester to RS, select an item with a tested pattern and set a small target such as one stack. Remove a few items and observe a replacement job and restored stock.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "SMALL STOCK TARGET: First make a successful manual craft of your basic processor pattern. Then ask Requestify to keep a target such as 16 in stock. Remove four, watch one replenishment job, and confirm the count settles back at the target.",
    "",
    "AVOID A LOOP: Do not export the entire target into a machine that returns it under the same rule. The requester sees the shortage and can schedule endless work. Choose a buffer and target you can explain.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Start with a modest target. Stockkeeping can consume all available ingredients if you configure many large targets at once."
  ],
  "task.6AC0DCA6EBB136CD.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.64DAE0DB64E14365.title": "Scale after measuring",
  "quest.64DAE0DB64E14365.quest_subtitle": "Autocrafting",
  "quest.64DAE0DB64E14365.quest_desc": [
    "ExtraStorage and Cable Tiers improve machine capacity and throughput. They are useful only after the underlying recipe and return path work.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Identify whether your bottleneck is pattern slots, transfer speed, machine speed or power. Inspect the relevant upgraded Autocrafter, Importer or Exporter in JEI and upgrade just that bottleneck.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A faster importer cannot speed up a slow furnace. Compare one timed batch before and after an upgrade."
  ],
  "task.0512854F690710D3.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.455FACFE88F00D4B.title": "Use fluids directly",
  "quest.455FACFE88F00D4B.quest_subtitle": "Resource Networks",
  "quest.455FACFE88F00D4B.quest_desc": [
    "Fluid substitution can avoid filling and emptying buckets for suitable recipes, but the stored fluid and the pattern must agree.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Choose a recipe supported by Refined Fluid Substitution. Read its pattern item/interface, provide the required fluid in network storage, then request a single test craft and inspect consumption.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Do not assume every bucket recipe supports substitution. Keep the original recipe available until the fluid-based version has succeeded."
  ],
  "task.27A4AA14DC0BEB2E.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.26D538689C43C6AC.title": "Refined Types: energy",
  "quest.26D538689C43C6AC.quest_subtitle": "Resource Networks",
  "quest.26D538689C43C6AC.quest_desc": [
    "Refined Types lets the network store additional resource types. An energy disk is a resource store; the RS Controller still needs operating power.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build an energy storage disk and fill it through a compatible resource input while the network has external power. The Network Energizer can then use stored FE to sustain the network itself; complete its side quest for that test.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "TWO POWER ROLES: Energy disks hold FE as a network resource. The Network Energizer lets the storage network use that stored FE for its own operating demand. A charged disk alone is not the same thing as an installed, active Energizer.",
    "",
    "USE THE ADDON: Bootstrap the network with ordinary external power and fill an energy disk through a compatible input. Add the Network Energizer, inspect its redstone mode, and confirm stored FE can sustain the network. Retain external power as a fallback while testing.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A disk stores energy; the Energizer makes that stored energy available for network operation. Keep external startup power available until this loop is proven."
  ],
  "task.403AA4D624A1AF07.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3736577BDC3D4F8E.title": "Refined Types: Source",
  "quest.3736577BDC3D4F8E.quest_subtitle": "Resource Networks",
  "quest.3736577BDC3D4F8E.quest_desc": [
    "Ars Nouveau Source is distinct from FE and ordinary fluid. It needs the relevant resource storage and a compatible connection.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Install a Source Storage Disk. Connect a small Ars Source supply using the supported interface, inspect the Source channel in the grid, then test extraction to a consumer.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "If no Source moves, check the connection's resource type and whether the neighboring block exposes a supported capability."
  ],
  "task.58987DD920E3CDE8.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3EC4CB893D60F0E4.title": "Refined Types: Souls",
  "quest.3EC4CB893D60F0E4.quest_subtitle": "Resource Networks",
  "quest.3EC4CB893D60F0E4.quest_desc": [
    "Industrial Foregoing Souls is another resource channel, not item experience or a mob stored in a Soul Vial.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect the Souls system in the Industrial Foregoing chapter first. Add a Soul Storage Disk when you have a real producer/consumer, then test one supported transfer in each direction.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A Regulator Upgrade can prevent an Exporter dumping all Souls into a connected soul pipe. This optional branch is not required for ordinary item autocrafting."
  ],
  "task.58555B618B61160C.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.277D7A61EC52AD2F.title": "Mekanism chemicals",
  "quest.277D7A61EC52AD2F.quest_subtitle": "Resource Networks",
  "quest.277D7A61EC52AD2F.quest_desc": [
    "Mekanism integration provides chemical storage and transfer. Chemical channels are separate from ordinary fluids and from Refined Types' Source.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Choose one chemical you already produce. Inspect the Mekanism integration disks and supported transfer settings, add suitable storage, and test a small transfer between the network and a machine.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use the machine's chemical-side configuration. A fluid pipe connection is not evidence that a chemical output is exposed."
  ],
  "task.464BD1B4A0619184.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.264F9DDB12C2AAF2.title": "One wireless workspace",
  "quest.264F9DDB12C2AAF2.quest_subtitle": "Wireless & Building",
  "quest.264F9DDB12C2AAF2.quest_desc": [
    "Universal Grid combines useful wireless network views; range and access still depend on your network equipment.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Charge and link a Universal Grid using its tooltip/interface, then test storage and crafting-monitor views near your transmitter. Add the installed interdimensional transmitter when ready for remote access.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Wireless access still needs a loaded, powered network. Test ordinary local access before crossing dimensions."
  ],
  "task.10201EB36E3C142B.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.65D2D38EC1C430A7.title": "Your inventory and the network",
  "quest.65D2D38EC1C430A7.quest_subtitle": "Wireless & Building",
  "quest.65D2D38EC1C430A7.quest_desc": [
    "Refined Wireless Upgrades adds convenience transfers and collection behavior. Powerful collection rules can also move things you meant to keep.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect its upgrades in JEI and choose one small convenience feature. Configure filters and test it with a few ordinary blocks before enabling it during an expedition.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Exclude tools, building reserves and special component-bearing items until you understand the transfer rules."
  ],
  "task.7BCF2949FFBE4794.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.4D7545E7E4FAE623.title": "Cook from storage",
  "quest.4D7545E7E4FAE623.quest_subtitle": "Wireless & Building",
  "quest.4D7545E7E4FAE623.quest_desc": [
    "Refined Cooking connects Cooking for Blockheads kitchens to RS ingredients, so food preparation can use your central supplies.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Place a Kitchen Station as part of the kitchen, a Kitchen Access Point on RS, and use the Kitchen Network Card to link them as described by their interfaces. Make one meal using stored ingredients.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Confirm the ordinary kitchen works first. A connected storage network cannot replace the kitchen blocks a recipe needs."
  ],
  "task.7B08C35D2D586FCB.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.3506A089BDA0396F.title": "Build from storage",
  "quest.3506A089BDA0396F.quest_subtitle": "Wireless & Building",
  "quest.3506A089BDA0396F.quest_desc": [
    "Refined Construction Sticks lets building tools draw blocks from RS. This reduces inventory refills while keeping construction intentional.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect the addon's items and the stick's tooltip, configure network access, and build a small wall using a known stored block. Watch both the placed result and the network count.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep a small manual supply until the connection is proven. Avoid testing with a rare decorative block or a huge placement area."
  ],
  "task.21E2669F65F61376.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.7212A4CE5FEDE709.title": "Supply a Schematicannon",
  "quest.7212A4CE5FEDE709.quest_subtitle": "Wireless & Building",
  "quest.7212A4CE5FEDE709.quest_desc": [
    "Refined Schematics adds a Cannon Interface to feed a Create Schematicannon from RS.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "First make a tiny Create schematic and verify a normal cannon setup. Add the Cannon Interface and configure its connection, stock the required blocks in RS, then run the small build.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Check the cannon's material list and build options before starting. A supply interface does not validate what the schematic will replace."
  ],
  "task.51FD3F8183180C41.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.67C1934FCABD1D48.title": "Search and capacity tools",
  "quest.67C1934FCABD1D48.quest_subtitle": "Wireless & Building",
  "quest.67C1934FCABD1D48.quest_desc": [
    "Search History saves repeated queries. Storage Warnings helps catch disk and storage-block capacity problems before inserts fail.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Use the grid search history to repeat a query. Inspect the warning triangle and per-resource settings. Compare free capacity for items, fluids and any extra resource channels you actually use.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "External storage is not included in the warning addon's capacity checks. Check drawer limits separately."
  ],
  "task.725A735FD7555F73.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.4B845A9FEBF30760.title": "Project: a small production cell",
  "quest.4B845A9FEBF30760.quest_subtitle": "Autocrafting",
  "quest.4B845A9FEBF30760.quest_desc": [
    "A reliable system combines a tested pattern, sufficient inputs, clear output return and sensible stock targets.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Automate one useful product through a real machine, keep a small stock with Requestify, access it wirelessly and demonstrate recovery from a missing-input condition. Write down the machine sides and return route.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep your existing RS basics chapter as reference. Expand only after this cell runs correctly through several batches."
  ],
  "task.1D64F70FC0809FF3.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.607A5690B41B5C79.title": "Three processor tiers",
  "quest.607A5690B41B5C79.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Autocrafting",
  "quest.607A5690B41B5C79.quest_desc": [
    "Basic, Improved and Advanced Processors recur throughout RS construction. Automating the raw-processor recipe and its smelting step makes later machines far less repetitive.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Start with the Basic Processor processing lesson. Extend the same tested pattern to the improved and advanced variants, then request four Advanced Processors in one job and verify that the monitor clears.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Each pattern must promise the actual cooked processor. A pattern for a raw processor does not automatically include the furnace step."
  ],
  "task.29C0A49A1DFF191D.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.512328E2927082A4.title": "Give machines a clean boundary",
  "quest.512328E2927082A4.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Autocrafting",
  "quest.512328E2927082A4.quest_desc": [
    "An Interface can provide a defined boundary between the network and external automation. A small buffer makes it easier to see what was delivered and what returned.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Place an Interface on a separate test branch, inspect its stocking/insertion controls and move a known item through it. Compare that behavior with an Importer before choosing how to return machine products.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Avoid two independent systems trying to stock and drain the same buffer. Assign one clear producer and one clear consumer."
  ],
  "task.7B23F8990F3B85A9.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.2166FAFC058F693D.title": "Energy is a resource type",
  "quest.2166FAFC058F693D.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Resource Networks",
  "quest.2166FAFC058F693D.quest_desc": [
    "The Network Energizer allows FE stored on energy disks to sustain the storage network. This connects the resource storage function to the network's operating cost.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Start with external power, charge a compatible energy disk, connect the Energizer and enable its redstone mode. Briefly remove the external feed and check that the network stays online while stored FE decreases; reconnect the feed afterward.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "An empty disk or inactive Energizer cannot sustain the network. Keep an accessible external supply so a failed bootstrap does not strand the test."
  ],
  "task.5957AC2723FB546C.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.024A45556BB0FA73.title": "Reach a second workshop",
  "quest.024A45556BB0FA73.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Wireless & Building",
  "quest.024A45556BB0FA73.quest_desc": [
    "A transmitter/receiver link extends a network without a continuous cable run. It still needs a correctly configured card and a powered, loaded destination.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Place a Network Receiver in a nearby second room, bind the Network Card as its tooltip describes, and put it into a connected Network Transmitter. Check a simple Grid at the receiver before moving farther away.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "First prove the link inside loaded chunks. Wireless access and chunk loading are separate problems."
  ],
  "task.349865DEC2BBD00E.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.01DBEC1918A4DFA4.title": "Share storage deliberately",
  "quest.01DBEC1918A4DFA4.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Wireless & Building",
  "quest.01DBEC1918A4DFA4.quest_desc": [
    "A shared world can have different access requirements for your main storage and public supplies. Security settings control the network; being an Essential friend does not explain every RS permission.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect the Security Manager and card permissions with your friend present. Test opening a Grid and inserting/removing a cheap item. Keep a way to restore the owner configuration before restricting access.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Change one permission at a time and test the intended account, rather than inferring friend access from what the owner can do."
  ],
  "task.3C7EEB1C7D0E3648.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.4859DAAFA0A04178.title": "A full output is a real test",
  "quest.4859DAAFA0A04178.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Autocrafting",
  "quest.4859DAAFA0A04178.quest_desc": [
    "A network that works only with empty buffers has not demonstrated reliable processing. Full output and absent ingredients are routine conditions, not rare accidents.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Use a cheap processing recipe, temporarily block its output and request one craft. Identify the waiting state in the monitor, restore space, and confirm the same job completes without cancelling and resubmitting it.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep the batch tiny. The point is to learn recovery, not to leave hundreds of promised items spread through machines."
  ]
}
